inees I would like to  explain the process that brought us to  today in both April and October the  makeup artist and hairstylist executive  committee meets and at this point we're  discussing certain business but they  also discuss the films that have been  released up through that period of time  these films are the committee that the  committee feels that all of the  membership should see so that as time  goes on they can continue those films or  if need be eliminate them a meeting is  then held in December for all of the  Academy makeup artists and hairstylists  branch members  to narrow down or add to the recommended  films to be seen january then becomes a  finalization month a really busy month  for all of the branch the first saturday  of january all members were asked to  attend a meeting to vote for the seven  films that will go on for consideration  not for nomination these are selected as  the seven best films for achievement in  makeup and hairstyling for the year I'd  like to point out how unbiased these  selections are as I read the seven films  that forty members in attendance chose  first we have Albert Nobbs filmed in  Ireland we have anonymous filmed in  Germany and England we have the artists  actually filmed in Hollywood filmed in  Hollywood by a French production company  with French actors then we have  gainsbourg a heroic life filmed in  France we have harry potter and the  deathly hallows part 2 filmed in england  and we have the iron lady filmed in  england as you can see seven great  accomplishments in the artistry of  makeup and hairstyling I would like to  point out from a non-biased standpoint  that of 15 possible nominees nine were  not Academy members and 12 were not  iatse local 706 members of the eight  final films three-on-three our Academy  are of the nominees three our Academy  members one lives in Los Angeles one in  New York and one in England the second  Saturday of January the makeup artists  and hairstylists executive commit